
Look over the simp_variant.c code and note:

1.) fun() is called 2 times. It is in the dispatch
    construct the second time.

2.) In the code blocks above main(), fun() is defined and is
    immediately preceeded by a declare_variant directive that
    specifies that the d_fun() function replaces fun() if it is in
    a dispatch (construct), which is the case for the second
    call to fun() in main.  The d_fun() executes a print
    statement on the default device through the target construct.

3.) The d_fun() is not a device function, per se, because it uses 
    a target construct within the function to perform offloading.
    In other cases, when a device binary is needed for the variant 
    function, it will be enclosed by a beginning and ending 
    declare_target directive (when in a separate compile unit).

4.) In C code, a forward defining prototype for d_fun() is required 
    since the declare_variant specifies the function as the 
    variant before it is defined.

